                                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
<h3>How much does Klaviyo cost in India for a D2C brand?</h3>
<p><strong>$20&ndash;$1,200+/mo</strong> depending on list size. USD billed (no INR option). At 10K contacts: ~$150/mo (~&#8377;12.5K). At 50K: ~$700/mo (~&#8377;58K).</p>
<h3>Is Brevo (Sendinblue) good enough for serious D2C ecommerce?</h3>
<p>Yes for most growth-stage brands. At &gt;30K contacts + Shopify, Klaviyo&rsquo;s segmentation + D2C templates start to materially outperform. Below that, Brevo is sufficient + 50&ndash;60% cheaper.</p>
<h3>Why did Mailchimp lose the D2C race?</h3>
<p><strong>Slow to add Shopify-native + D2C automation features.</strong> Klaviyo built D2C-first; Mailchimp built newsletter-first then bolted ecommerce on. Result: D2C brands moved to Klaviyo for retention; Mailchimp lost majority of ecommerce market 2020&ndash;2024.</p>
<h3>Can I do WhatsApp + email from one tool?</h3>
<p><strong>Brevo</strong> natively. <strong>Klaviyo</strong>: email + SMS native, WhatsApp via separate tool (Klaviyo + WATI / Interakt). <strong>Mailchimp</strong>: email + SMS only.</p>
<h3>How long does it take to switch email platforms?</h3>
<p><strong>3&ndash;6 weeks</strong> for clean migration: list export, contact upload, segment recreation, flow rebuild, template migration, A/B testing dial-in. Plan for 4&ndash;8 weeks of dual-running to validate before sunsetting old platform.</p>
<h3>Should I use Klaviyo Reviews + Klaviyo SMS or separate tools?</h3>
<p><strong>Klaviyo Reviews</strong>: skip; better dedicated tools exist (Junip, Yotpo). <strong>Klaviyo SMS</strong>: yes &mdash; native integration into segments + flows is the best in market for D2C.</p>


